    pjm_demand_response_supply: { cell: ".", fc: "K", ev: "OWNER RULING 2026-09-05 (in-session, on the capx D57 A/B; FINDING-capx-d57-2026-09-05.md section 8): ARMED FOR PJM as part of the JOINT configuration (pjm_accreditation_design_vintage + this field + capacity_market_supply_clearing_by_iso[PJM]) through iso_configs.py::_pjm_config default_scenario_overrides; the ScenarioConfig default stays False (every other ISO and every backcast keeper byte-identical; --no-pjm-demand-response-supply reaches the control). Prior record: capx D48 Phase 1 (2026-09-04), FINDING-capx-d48-2026-09-04.md -- MEASURED WITH pjm_accreditation_design_vintage in the one A/B arm pjm-t1h-d48-devintage (key bbe13b3f7b659d36), DEFAULT-OFF, NOT ARMED. Zero-solve decomposition on the post-D44 D45-R ledgers: counting the published OFFERED DR UCAP (10,513 / 10,117 / 10,146 / 6,085 MW in 2022-2025) as supply with the peak un-netted moves the entering position UP +3.25 / +3.03 / +2.93 / +0.26 pt (AWAY from the published cleared position, the pre-declared sign) and enlarges the pipeline admission cap's firm-MW exit budget by +5.1 GW in 2022-2024 -- the D half, not the V half, carries almost all of the budget growth that admitted +1.4 GW more coal into the 2022 exit cohort (FC-3 retire.total_gw 17.958 -> 19.361). Convention reading for the owner (this row's question): OFFERED DR exceeds CLEARED DR by 2.0-2.5 GW in 2022/23-2024/25 (BRA Tables 3A/6), so counting the offered series is the census-vs-cleared choice on the demand side exactly as the generation census is on the supply side; the netting the shipped posture uses (ADEQUACY_DEMAND_RESPONSE_FRACTION_BY_ISO, 3.97 % of peak ~ 5.9 GW) sits nearer the cleared quantity. The section-5 flip condition fails on limb (a) for the paired arm; nothing arms; O stays O; a D-only probe (key c79fc92aaaac53cc) is NOT solved." },
    capacity_market_supply_clearing: { cell: ".", fc: "K", ev: "capx D57 (2026-09-05), BUILT from DESIGN-capx-d54-pjm-clearing-half-2026-09-05.md and MEASURED (FINDING-capx-d57-2026-09-05.md). Phase 0: the code's clear_capacity_supply_stack reproduces the D54 instrument to 0.000 $/MW-day and 0.000 pt on both bases (docs/handoffs/d57/phase0-reproduction-2026-09-05.*). A/B, PJM solo, years sequential (14.0 / 13.4 min, 9.1 / 9.3 GB): arm A pjm-2021-2025-realized-t1h-d57-clearing (D48 both fields + clearing; key f0e050e820c1159a, pre-declared and matched) and arm B -headbasis (clearing on HEAD's basis; ccee17a4c1563727) vs the census control (D45-R, c6091bd5b62bbc3f) and pjm-t1h-d48-devintage. MEASURED -- the QUANTITY: cleared position within -0.48 / -0.98 / -2.79 pts (A; B -0.98 / -1.29 / -3.18) of the published BRA cleared position for 2022/23-2024/25 where the census sat +8.5 / +4.1 / -4.3 pts away; the section-3.5 identity (failing set == uncleared set) HOLDS in all eight solved screens; 2025/26 short => census exactly (I1 live). The PRICE: 76.10 / 82.81 / 165.84 $/MW-day (A) = 1.52x / 2.43x / 5.73x the published 50.00 / 34.13 / 28.92 (B 1.92x / 2.81x / 6.35x), set by a marginal offer in every long year, never inside the +/-20 % falsifier: the gas-CT (404 units / 24.2 GW firm), gas-ST (115 / 8.8 GW) and oil (421 / 3.7 GW) fleets offer at their FULL bars (zero E&AS in the hindcast prices) -- an E&AS margin of >= 3.8 / 18.0 / 8.6 $/kW-yr per CT / ST / oil unit (2022/23, UCAP basis) would put those offers AT the published price; measured, never moved (rule 21). FC-3 (both arms converge): retire.total 18.70 GW (control 17.96, D48 arm 19.36, actual 15.06; FAIL), coal 6.02 (economic 11.4 -> 0.44 GW: the cohort clears at the formed price and REVERSES -- the D48 +1.4 GW retained and more), gas_st 10.30 (economic 9.47 vs 2.7 actual: every zero-E&AS steam unit is uncleared and paid $0), gas_cc 2.33, recall 17 -> 12/20 (FAIL), false_retire 6.69 -> 9.49, +4.0 GW gas_cc entry in the 2023 screen (the entry screen reads the $28.7/kW-yr clearing price as a price taker and a new CC clears its LCOE), HOLD both. The admission cap's pool falls from 89 GW failing at $0 to the 19-21 GW uncleared set (it trims 37-42 % of it, coal-and-steam first; floor_retained 0 every year). Pre-declaration graded 14 HIT / 4 SPLIT / 6 MISS, every miss the operand's signature exceeding its own band (PREDECL-capx-d57 sections 4-5). OWNER RULING 2026-09-05 (in-session, on this measured A/B; finding section 8): ARMED FOR PJM -- the JOINT configuration (pjm_accreditation_design_vintage + pjm_demand_response_supply + this gate) is PJM's shipped forecast posture through iso_configs.py::_pjm_config default_scenario_overrides (the three ScenarioConfig defaults stay off; every other ISO and every backcast keeper byte-identical; an explicit --no-... reaches the D45-R control). The bare pjm-t1h verdict key is arm A's f0e050e820c1159a; D45-R's census leg is preserved at pjm-t1h-pre-d57. Accepted on rule 1 [R-STRUCT] with the FC-3 COMPOSITION cost stated; the named successor is the CT / ST / oil E&AS operand (the D12 scarcity-basis lane). The PJM T1-F bundle (pjm-2026-2030-d45r-remeasure) now carries a SUPERSEDED posture and joins the director's batched re-measure (the D44 precedent)." },
